---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import PostCard from '../../components/PostCard.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { readingTime } from '../../lib/reading-time';

const RELEVANT_TAGS = ['agentic-ai', 'mcp', 'context-management', 'product-engineering'];

const relatedPosts = (await getCollection('blog'))
  .filter((p) => p.data.tags.some((t) => RELEVANT_TAGS.includes(t)))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.publishDate.getTime() - a.data.publishDate.getTime())
  .slice(0, 3);

const pricing = [
  { name: 'AI Transformation Strategy', detail: 'A focused session, written recommendation, credits forward', price: '$900' },
  { name: 'AI Readiness / Discovery Sprint', detail: '2 weeks, remote-first, fixed fee', price: '$8,500' },
  { name: 'Agentic workflow pilot', detail: 'Single use case, 4–8 weeks, scoped', price: '$25,000–$50,000' },
  { name: 'Ongoing retainer', detail: '~20 hrs/mo, 3-month minimum', price: '$6,000/mo' },
  { name: 'Fractional AI leadership', detail: 'Up to 3 days/week, scoped', price: 'from $10,000/mo' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Business Process Automation"
  description="Automate the repetitive work your team does by hand — intake, triage, reporting, follow-ups — with reliable, verified automation that's still running in six months."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main>
    <Hero
      eyebrow="Service 02"
      title="Automate your <em>business processes.</em>"
      subtitle="The repetitive work your team does by hand — intake, triage, reporting, follow-ups — designed into automation that runs reliably and gets checked before anything ships. Built on the same agentic tooling I write about, without you needing to care what it's called."
      primaryCta={{ href: '/contact', label: 'Get in touch' }}
      secondaryCta={{ href: '/work', label: 'See the work' }}
      size="md"
      markImage="/images/services/agentic-workflows.webp"
    />

    <section class="section section--tight who">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
        <h2 class="who__title">Two people, one root cause</h2>
        <div class="who__grid">
          <div class="who__card card" data-reveal>
            <span class="card-tag">01</span>
            <h3>The ops leader drowning in manual triage</h3>
            <p>
              Someone on your team is copy-pasting between three tools every morning, manually routing tickets or
              reconciling records, and calling it "the job" because it's always been the job. It doesn't have to be.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="who__card card" data-reveal>
            <span class="card-tag">02</span>
            <h3>The founder who wants a pilot that ships</h3>
            <p>
              You've seen a slick agent demo. You want the version that survives contact with real data, real edge
              cases, and a real production environment — not another proof of concept that quietly dies in a repo.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section villain grid-ground" data-reveal>
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">The failure mode</p>
        <h2 class="villain__title">The pilot that never ships</h2>
        <p class="villain__text">
          Here's the villain of this whole category: an agent that works great in the demo, gets a round of applause,
          and then never touches production because nobody built a way to know when it's wrong. It has no
          verification loop, no owner, no path from "looks good in the recording" to "runs unattended on Tuesday."
          Six months later it's a slide in a deck nobody opens. I don't build those.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tight happens">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">What happens</p>
        <h2 class="happens__title">Verification loop first, automation second</h2>
        <Prose>
          <p>
            Every engagement starts by finding the check, not the prompt. Before I write a single agent step, I
            establish how we'll know the output is correct — a test harness, a human-in-the-loop review gate, a
            comparison against ground truth, or an automated eval suite scoped to your actual data. That
            verification loop is the spine everything else hangs off of.
          </p>
          <p>
            From there I build the smallest version of the pipeline that can run end-to-end against real inputs,
            not sample data. It's instrumented from day one — logging what it did, why, and how confident it was —
            so failures are visible instead of silent. We run it in shadow mode alongside the manual process until
            the numbers earn trust, then cut over.
          </p>
          <p>
            The stack is chosen for what the problem needs, not what's trending — sometimes that's an MCP server
            wired into your existing tools, sometimes it's a plain scheduled job with an LLM call in the middle of
            it. The agent framework is the least interesting part of this. The verification loop is the part that
            decides whether it's still running next quarter.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tight walkaway grid-ground">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you walk away with</p>
        <h2 class="walkaway__title">A working pipeline, not a slide deck</h2>
        <ul class="walkaway__list">
          <li data-reveal>
            <h3>A pipeline running in production</h3>
            <p>Deployed against your real systems, handling your real inputs — not a sandboxed demo environment.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <h3>A verification loop your team can maintain</h3>
            <p>Documented, instrumented, and owned by someone on your team — not dependent on me staying on retainer forever.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <h3>A written account of what it can't do yet</h3>
            <p>Every agent has edges. You'll know exactly where they are instead of finding out from an angry customer.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tight pricing">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">How pricing works</p>
        <h2 class="pricing__title">Real numbers, not a contact form</h2>
        <div class="pricing__table-wrap">
          <table class="pricing__table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Engagement</th>
                <th>Detail</th>
                <th>Price</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {pricing.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{row.name}</td>
                  <td>{row.detail}</td>
                  <td class="pricing__price">{row.price}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="pricing__philosophy">
          Most engagements start with a short AI transformation strategy session — a focused conversation and a
          written recommendation, credited toward whatever comes next. Remote work is priced the same as the work;
          on-site carries a day-rate premium plus travel at cost, never a surprise change order. These are real
          numbers, not a "contact us" form.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {relatedPosts.length > 0 && (
      <section class="section section--tight related">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p>
          <h2 class="related__title">From the blog</h2>
          <div class="related__grid">
            {relatedPosts.map((post) => (
              <PostCard
                title={post.data.title}
                description={post.data.description}
                publishDate={post.data.publishDate}
                tags={post.data.tags}
                slug={post.id}
                readingTime={readingTime(post.body ?? '')}
              />
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    )}

    <CtaBand title="Bring the workflow that's actually broken." />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .who__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-md); }
  .who__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-sm); }
  .who__card h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin: 0.5rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .who__card p { color: var(--color-muted); }

  .villain__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-md); }
  .villain__text {
    max-width: 64ch;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  .happens__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-md); }

  .walkaway__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-lg); }
  .walkaway__list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-lg); }
  .walkaway__list li { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); padding-top: var(--space-sm); }
  .walkaway__list h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .walkaway__list p { color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 42ch; }

  .pricing__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-md); }
  .pricing__table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .pricing__table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .pricing__table th,
  .pricing__table td {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: 0.65em 0.85em;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .pricing__table th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .pricing__table td { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .pricing__price { font-family: var(--font-mono); white-space: nowrap; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .pricing__philosophy { color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 64ch; }

  .related__title { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0.5rem 0 var(--space-md); }
  .related__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-md); }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .who__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .walkaway__list { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .related__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .related__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
